lesson: 150
title: A square cut into equal strips
level: primary-3
stars: 3
explain: When a square is cut by parallel cuts into equal strips, every strip is as long as the square's side, and its width is the side divided by the number of strips.
explain: So the perimeter of a strip is two sides of the square and two widths: if there are 3 strips, the half-perimeter of a strip is one side and one third of a side, that is 4 thirds of the side.
explain: For 3 strips with a perimeter of 16 cm each: half is 8 cm = 4 widths, so a width is 2 cm, the side is 3 × 2 = 6 cm and the square's perimeter is 4 × 6 = 24 cm.
vars: a=name k=2..6 u=2..12
let: s = k * u
let: p = 2 * (s + u)
need: s <= 60
answer: 4 * s
exercise: A square piece of paper is cut into {k} equal strips. The perimeter of each strip is {p} cm. What was the perimeter of the square?
exercise: {k} equal rectangles are put side by side, without gaps, and they make a square. Each rectangle has a perimeter of {p} cm. What is the perimeter of the square?
exercise: A square garden is divided by straight paths into {k} equal rectangular beds, all lying side by side. The perimeter of each bed is {p} m. What is the perimeter of the whole garden in metres?
exercise: A square is cut into {k} equal rectangles. The perimeters of all the rectangles add up to {k*p} cm. What is the perimeter of the square?
exercise: {a} folded a square sheet into {k} equal strips and cut along the folds. Every strip has a perimeter of {p} cm. Find the perimeter of the square sheet.
test: {a} lays {k} identical rectangular tiles in a row and gets a square. The perimeter of one tile is {p} cm. Find the perimeter of the square.
test: A square is cut parallel to one of its sides into {k} equal rectangles. The perimeter of every rectangle is {p} cm. How long is the edge all around the square?
test: A square sheet of plywood is sawn into {k} equal long pieces. If you go round all the pieces one by one, you measure {k*p} cm in all. What was the perimeter of the whole sheet?
exercise: A square tablecloth is cut into {k} equal strips. Each strip has a perimeter of {p} cm. What is the perimeter of the tablecloth in centimetres?
exercise: When {k} identical rectangles are laid side by side, they form a square. The perimeter of every rectangle is {p} cm. Find the perimeter of the square.
exercise: A square field in Iowa is split by fences into {k} equal strips that run from one side to the other. Every strip has a perimeter of {p} m. What is the perimeter of the field in metres?
exercise: What was the perimeter of a square that was cut into {k} equal strips, each with a perimeter of {p} cm?
exercise: {a} cuts a square of card into {k} equal strips. The perimeters of the strips, added together, come to {k*p} cm. What was the perimeter of the card?
exercise: A square bar of chocolate is broken into {k} equal long bars. The edge of each bar measures {p} mm all round. How many millimetres is the edge of the whole square bar?
exercise: A square patio in Adelaide is made of {k} equal rectangular slabs laid side by side. The perimeter of one slab is {p} dm. What is the perimeter of the patio in decimetres?
exercise: A square sheet is cut with straight parallel cuts into {k} strips of the same size. Each strip measures {p} cm around. What is the perimeter of the sheet?
test: The perimeter of each of {k} equal strips is {p} cm. The strips were cut from one square. What was that square's perimeter?
test: A square quilt in Dublin is sewn from {k} equal rectangular panels in a row. A single panel has a perimeter of {p} cm. How long is the edge of the whole quilt, in centimetres?
test: {a} saws a square board into {k} matching planks, cutting parallel to one edge. Each plank is {p} cm round. How many centimetres is the board's perimeter?
test: A square garden in Surrey is made of {k} identical beds side by side. Walking round every bed once, one after another, a gardener walks {k*p} m in all. How long is the fence round the whole garden?
test: What is the perimeter of a square if {k} identical strips cut from it have perimeters of {p} cm each?
test: A square window in a church in Wales is made of {k} equal panes in a row. The frame round each pane is {p} cm long. How long is the outer edge of the window, in centimetres?
