exam: It is given that a square sheet of paper is divided into {k.words} congruent rectangular strips, each strip possessing a perimeter of {p} cm. Determine the perimeter of the original square in centimetres.
exam: Whereas {k} identical rectangles, each of perimeter {p} cm, are juxtaposed without interstices so as to constitute a square, compute the perimeter of the square so formed, in centimetres.
exam: Ascertain, in centimetres, the perimeter of a square which, upon being cut by parallel lines into {k} equal strips, yields strips each of a perimeter of {p} cm.
exam: A square tile is partitioned into {k.words} equal rectangles by cuts parallel to one of its sides, the perimeter of each rectangle being {p} cm. State the perimeter of the tile, expressed in centimetres.
exercise: Grandma's old square tablecloth didn't make it through the wash, so {a} cuts it into {k} equal strips for rags. Each strip has a perimeter of {p} cm. What was the perimeter of the tablecloth?
exercise: When Rex crossed the rainbow bridge, {a} cut his square blanket into {k} equal strips. Each strip has a perimeter of {p} cm. What was the perimeter of the blanket?
